User cannot access the shared drive to their department from their remote workstation:

Issue Description:
I can't get to my files on the Marketing shared drive today. I keep getting "The network path was not found" when I try to open it. 
I'm working from home today. My internet and email both work fine.

Troubleshooting performed by user:
- Restarted my computer (no change)
- Internet and email work normally
- The mapped drives say disconnected

The first thing to research is whether the user is connected to the VPN.
By remote accessing their device, we can see their VPN client and if it's on Disconnected/offline, we will press the button to connect.

We will then check with the user if they can connect after this.
If not, proceed to the next step.

We will open the tools for documentation and file server where we will find the Marketing UNC(Universal Naming Convention) path:
\\FILESERV01\departments\Marketing - Marketing department files

With this information, we will not re-visit the users PC remote and open the file explorer -> This PC -> ... -> Map network drive

A box will show up with the Drive letter, in our case: D:
And a box to write in a folder directory.
This is where the \\FILESERV01\departments\Marketing will be written in. And then I click finish.

This more often will solve the problem, and in this case, the ticket got solved!
